{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     training.hbs — the index of training SECTIONS.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     NS-Design-System's training-index archetype. Sections are rendered as
     `.ns-trackcard` — the numbered form — because training is an ORDER: you
     go through it. Courses use `.ns-path__card`, the glyph-led form, because
     a course is a destination you pick. That is the whole difference between
     the two catalogues and it is deliberate.

     ── Three levels of navigation across two levels of URL ────────────────
         /training/                  this page — every section
         /training/{section}/        the section, listing its posts
         /training/{section}/{post}/ a post

     `abstract/18` is explicit that Ghost gives a permalink exactly one
     `{primary_tag}` placeholder, so there is no third URL level available.
     This page is the third level of NAVIGATION without being a third level of
     URL — which is why it is a collection root rather than a tag.

     `posts` here is the collection: the section overview posts, filtered by
     `tag:hash-training-module` in routes.yaml and ordered by published_at.
     Backdate a section post to move it earlier; that is the whole ordering
     mechanism, and it is what makes the numerals on these cards mean
     something.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    <div class="ns-band__head">
      <p class="ns-kicker">{{t "Training"}}</p>
      {{#page}}
        <h1 class="ns-band__title">{{title}}</h1>
        {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-band__lede">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
      {{else}}
        <h1 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Training"}}</h1>
        <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "A guided path, in order. Each section builds on the one before it."}}</p>
      {{/page}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ns-band">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    {{#if posts}}
      <div class="ns-grid">
        {{#foreach posts}}{{> "home/track-card" index=@number}}{{/foreach}}
      </div>
    {{else}}
      {{!-- A site with no training yet. Say what is missing rather than
            rendering an empty grid. --}}
      <p class="ns-empty">{{t "No training sections yet."}}</p>
    {{/if}}

    {{pagination}}
  </div>
</section>
